t_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1AToiIbbwT", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 904, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8941295, "raw_content": "", "author": "Landslide_2020", "created": 1794771623783, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "Washington_Redskins", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "thepostmillennial.com", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "https://media.scored.co/preview/1AToiIbbwT.png", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://thepostmillennial.com/news/us-vet-heads-to-canada-for-free-health-care-is-offered-government-assisted-death-instead", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "It's Canada, what did she expect \ud83e\udd14?  A U.S. veteran with Ovarian cancer and her husband moved to Canada in hopes of avoiding the financial costs of the U.S. Healthcare system.  Instead, she was offered Assisted Murder (Suicide). ", "last_comment_created": 1794821705457, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 127, "score_up": 904, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"description": "Kirstin Logan and her husband, Donovan James, moved to Canada in hopes of avoiding the financial costs of the US healthcare system in the US.", "large_image": "slZxwNZdNgrFZjbT.png", "title": "US vet heads to Canada for free health care \u2014 is offered government-assisted death instead"}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "text", "uuid": "1AToiJkHFD", "is_twitter": false, "is_admin": false, "score": 17, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8942353, "raw_content": "**THE MAGA TAKEOVER: HOW THE REPUBLICAN OLD GUARD COULD LOSE CONTROL**\n\nIf MAGA intends to replace the Republican establishment and fundamentally challenge the globalist international order, winning the White House alone is not enough.\n\nThe Republican Party is an institution with its own leadership, committees, donors, rules, and political machinery. Controlling the presidency does not automatically mean controlling the party.\n\n**The real battlegrounds are:**\n\n1. **Republican primaries:** Incumbents can be challenged by candidates who offer a different foreign-policy and economic agenda. Ultimately, Republican voters decide.\n\n2. **State party leadership:** State chairs, county committees, and local party organizations exercise significant influence over party operations and leadership selection.\n\n3. **Precincts and conventions:** In states that use caucuses and conventions, grassroots party participation influences who becomes a delegate and who holds internal authority.\n\n4. **The RNC:** National committee leadership, party rules, and delegate procedures shape the party's direction beyond any single presidential administration.\n\n5. **Political financing:** Donor networks, PACs, and independent political organizations influence which candidates can mount competitive campaigns. Their activities remain subject to election law.\n\n6. **Congress:** Even a president with overwhelming grassroots support needs congressional votes to enact legislation, approve budgets, and reshape American foreign policy.\n\n7. **Institutional accountability:** Candidates who campaign against interventionism, entrenched lobbying, or international institutions can be judged against their voting records and actions in office.\n\n**The constitutional limit matters:** An elected government can pursue major changes to foreign policy, trade agreements, international commitments, and federal priorities. It cannot legitimately use government power to punish political opponents merely for belonging to the old guard.\n\n**THE BOTTOM LINE**\n\nThe Republican establishment cannot be replaced simply by winning one election. Lasting control depends on who wins nominations, who governs party institutions, who commands congressional support, and who can sustain an electoral majority.\n\nA genuine political realignment is accomplished through legitimate political competition, not by treating disagreement as grounds for state punishment.", "author": "HowCome", "created": 1794849200602, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "texas4ever", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "", "removal_source": "", "link": "", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "MAGA needs to take control of the Republican party. There needs to be a rule. You must be openly hostile to the cause of Globalism and the Globalist World Order Financial System to get our Votes. If Only.", "last_comment_created": 1794851238808, "content": "<p><strong>THE MAGA TAKEOVER: HOW THE REPUBLICAN OLD GUARD COULD LOSE CONTROL</strong></p>\n<p>If MAGA intends to replace the Republican establishment and fundamentally challenge the globalist international order, winning the White House alone is not enough.</p>\n<p>The Republican Party is an institution with its own leadership, committees, donors, rules, and political machinery. Controlling the presidency does not automatically mean controlling the party.</p>\n<p><strong>The real battlegrounds are:</strong></p>\n<ol>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Republican primaries:</strong> Incumbents can be challenged by candidates who offer a different foreign-policy and economic agenda. Ultimately, Republican voters decide.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>State party leadership:</strong> State chairs, county committees, and local party organizations exercise significant influence over party operations and leadership selection.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Precincts and conventions:</strong> In states that use caucuses and conventions, grassroots party participation influences who becomes a delegate and who holds internal authority.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>The RNC:</strong> National committee leadership, party rules, and delegate procedures shape the party's direction beyond any single presidential administration.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Political financing:</strong> Donor networks, PACs, and independent political organizations influence which candidates can mount competitive campaigns. Their activities remain subject to election law.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Congress:</strong> Even a president with overwhelming grassroots support needs congressional votes to enact legislation, approve budgets, and reshape American foreign policy.</p>\n</li>\n<li>\n<p><strong>Institutional accountability:</strong> Candidates who campaign against interventionism, entrenched lobbying, or international institutions can be judged against their voting records and actions in office.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<p><strong>The constitutional limit matters:</strong> An elected government can pursue major changes to foreign policy, trade agreements, international commitments, and federal priorities. It cannot legitimately use government power to punish political opponents merely for belonging to the old guard.</p>\n<p><strong>THE BOTTOM LINE</strong></p>\n<p>The Republican establishment cannot be replaced simply by winning one election. Lasting control depends on who wins nominations, who governs party institutions, who commands congressional support, and who can sustain an electoral majority.</p>\n<p>A genuine political realignment is accomplished through legitimate political competition, not by treating disagreement as grounds for state punishment.</p>\n", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 8, "score_up": 17, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"status": 200}, "post_flair_text": "", "archive_id": ""}, {"is_locked": false, "tweet_id": "2122150777007599630", "sticky_comment": 0, "is_video_mp4": false, "type": "link", "uuid": "1AToiJjj53", "is_twitter": true, "is_admin": false, "score": 29, "suggested_sort": 0, "post_flair_class": "", "id": 8942145, "raw_content": "", "author": "kek_saved_the_world", "created": 1794838383183, "profile_picture": "", "community": "TheDonald", "ad_tier": 2, "last_comment_author": "GoodvsEvil2", "is_video": false, "video_link": "", "is_new_user": false, "domain": "twitter.com", "is_crosspost": false, "preview": "https://media.scored.co/preview/1AToiJjj53.png", "removal_source": "", "link": "https://twitter.com/HeritageUSA__/status/2122150777007599630", "author_flair_class": "", "is_removed": false, "media": {"resized_resolutions": [], "blurhash": "", "full_resolution": []}, "title": "Notice how much aura the white players have over the gay shit at the front.\n\nThe rap era is falling off a cliff because black culture isn't cool anymore, it looks ridiculous and gay.", "last_comment_created": 1794846369018, "content": "", "score_down": 0, "author_flair_text": "", "pro_tier": 0, "is_stickied": false, "is_nsfw": false, "is_deleted": false, "is_image": false, "comments": 5, "score_up": 29, "is_edited": false, "is_moderator": false, "awards": 0, "vote_state": 2, "link_metadata": {"twitter": {"quotedTweet": false, "images": false, "linkEmbed": false, "replies": 409, "created": 1794795147000, "id": "2122150777007599630", "video": {"preview": "https://pbs.twimg.com/amplify_video_thumb/2122075569806315522/img/DilkAE8Drv6dC2LO.jpg", "mpeg": "https://video.twimg.com/amplify_video/2122075569806315522/pl/WRI6fqGRdfxHj_ax.m3u8?v=f9f", "aspectRatio": [9, 16], "heightRatio": 177, "type": "video/mp4", "url": "https://video.tw